        "math_academy_id": "q-74603",
        "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=0 \\\\  & 3x-2y+6z=-1 \\\\  & -2x+2y-z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
        "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
